<% content_for :title, "Lab" %>

<h1>Lab</h1>
<p class="text-muted">
  What the runners are doing right now. The status below updates in place every 30 seconds
  — the page itself never reloads, so it never loses your place.
</p>

<%# The frame refetches itself: nothing outside it moves, so the poll controller is scoped
    to the frame and only ever calls its reload(). Eager, not lazy: Turbo drops a lazy
    frame's reload() until its very first load has settled, so an early refetch — the tab
    coming back moments after the page opened — would silently do nothing. %>
<turbo-frame id="lab_status" src="<%= lab_status_path %>"
             data-controller="frame-poll" data-frame-poll-interval-value="30000">
  <p class="text-muted">Loading status…</p>
</turbo-frame>
